      "right": {
        "headline": "Good: say what a field is",
        "body": "Greedy .* takes everything it can. A character class says exactly what a username may contain."
      },
      "gaps": {
        "headline": "Right, with gaps",
        "body": "The result is right; it went late, unchecked, before you looked, or with a weaker fix than the cause called for."
      },
      "wrongSent": {
        "headline": "Wrong report",
        "body": "Anchoring a greedy group on the next word still overreaches when that word repeats."
      },
      "notSent": {
        "headline": "Nothing shipped",
        "body": "Safe, but the deadline passed without the fix."
      },
      "time_up": {
        "headline": "Time up",
        "body": "Nothing was recorded before the case's limit."
      }
    },
    "modelReasoning": "Usernames that carry the rest of the line point at the pattern. In user=(.*) followed by a space, .* is greedy: it consumes as much as possible and backs off only to the last space, so the group captures the ip field too. Describe the field instead: user=(?P<user>[^ ]+) with named groups for ip and result, anchored to the line format. A lazy .*? works on clean lines but accepts empty names; anchoring on ' ip' fails when ip= appears twice. Check the counts against the VPN console."
  }
